ic information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Linking Words with the Same Consonant Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Linking words with the same consonant sounds smoothly connect one word to the next when speaking. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If a word that ends in a consonant sound is immediately followed by another word that starts with the same consonant sound,  you pronounce  the two consonants as one sound.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice pronouncing the linking words in the following examples.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":6,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"P-P\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"G-G\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"D-D\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"T-T\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"R-R\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"K-C\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" step parent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Big girl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" red dish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" get ten\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" wear red\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" dark color\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ste<span class=\\\"strong\\\">p</span>arent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bi<span class=\\\"strong\\\">g</span>irl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"re<span class=\\\"strong\\\">d</span>ish\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ge<span class=\\\"strong\\\">t</span>en\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wea<span class=\\\"strong\\\">r</span>ed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dar<span class=\\\"strong\\\">c</span>olor\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'm a big girl, but for me, meeting someone in a club is unthinkable. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He wore big glasses, some makeup and dark colored clothes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hi, do you speak Korean?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Pronunciating words with -able", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "One of the most common suffixes is -able. This changes a verb to an adjective.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you remove -able from a word, you are left with a complete word (breakable, break).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">-able is pronounced /\u0259bl/</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You stress the 'a' that comes right before 'ble'", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To think -     think-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble<br/>To believe -  believe-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say these words. Stress the bolded syllable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">replace-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;reli-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">believe-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;                           think-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">imagine-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;                         like-<span class=\"strong\">a</span>-ble</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Add the prefix -un:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-replace-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-reli-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-believe-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-imagine-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" un-think-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"un-like-<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a</span>-ble\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The prefix -un does not change the stress, it changes the meaning of the word.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My weekend was an unbelievable event. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had an unimaginable  Saturday evening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Meeting someone in a club is unthinkable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He was not unlikeable.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unbelievable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unlikely or difficult to believe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My weekend was an unbelievable event.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you talk about attraction!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unlikeable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not likely to be liked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He was not unlikeable ... at all.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unthinkable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "impossible to conceive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Meeting someone in a club is unthinkable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to glance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look quickly or briefly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, when I was talking to my friend, you glanced over.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to melt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to soften someone's feelings and emotions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I melted. It was magical. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "couldn't take my eyes off of someone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used when it is hard to stop looking at someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  We talked some more, but I couldn't take my eyes off him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "love at first sight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a feeling of warm personal attachment or deep affection ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As soon as I saw him I melted. I believe it was love at first sight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Students brainstorm some famous celebrities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In pairs, create some questions about personal experiences that  you would like to ask a celebrity. Also ask how long they have been doing various things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch pairs, one student is a famous celebrity and one is a reporter.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The reporter questions the celebrity and the celebrity answers. The reporter should respond using target vocabulary like unbelievable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch partners.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I say and use words like unbelievable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I pronounce questions like \"How long have you been ...\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can develop questions about experience.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn8le16ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "My weekend was an unbelievable event. I had an unimaginable &nbsp;Saturday evening.<br/>\nI went out to dinner, I went to a costume party at a dance club. At the club, I met the most amazing man. Now, I&rsquo;m a big girl, but for me, meeting someone in a club is unthinkable.<br/>", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn8le16ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "I was dressed as a cat and I was having a great time dancing with Steve when I heard someone behind me talking in a strange language. I turned around and looked and I saw the most handsome man I had ever seen. He looked just like Bruce Lee. His costume was unusual. He wore big glasses, some makeup and dark colored clothes. I walked back to the table and when Steve went to the bathroom, Bruce Lee came over. He leaned in and asked me, &ldquo;Hi, do you speak Korean?&rdquo;<br/>\n&ldquo; Ah ... No.&rdquo;<br/>\n&ldquo;Well, when I was talking to my friend, you glanced over. I thought maybe you spoke Korean.&rdquo;<br/>", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn8le16ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "I smiled. Then he asked me some questions like:<br/>\n&ldquo;How long have you been such a good dancer?&rdquo; &ldquo;How long have you been a fan of cats?&rdquo; &nbsp;He asked me what I did and I told him I wrote a blog. Then he asked, &ldquo;How long have you been doing that?&rdquo; We talked some more, but I couldn&rsquo;t take my eyes off him. &nbsp;He was not unlikeable ... at all. Finally, he smiled that amazing smile and asked, &ldquo;How long have you been this beautiful?&rdquo;<br/>\nI melted. It was magical.<br/>", "id": 3, "time": "55500", "image": "engenn8le16ob04re2img05.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le16ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le16ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say and use words like unbelievable.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can pronounce questions like \"<span class=\"italic\">How long have you been ... </span>\"", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can pronounce words with the same consonant sound.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you believe in love at first sight? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How long have you believed in love at first sight?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_h